 "intro": "Abritus (near Razgrad, Bulgaria), summer 251 AD. The Goths are heading home from sacking Philippopolis. You are the Emperor Decius, with your son Herennius Etruscus.",
 "debrief": "In Jordanes’s and other accounts, Decius caught the Goths near Abritus. His son was killed by an arrow early on, and Decius is said to have told his men the loss of one soldier mattered little. Two Gothic lines broke, but the Romans chased them into a marsh where the third line waited. Decius and much of his army died; his body was never found. He was the first emperor killed by a foreign enemy. Trebonianus Gallus let the Goths go home. The other choices are what-ifs.",
